    "result_text": "All tests pass (4 tests, 2 test classes \u2014 the complete suite) and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the salutation feature following the project's established Spring/MapStruct/OpenAPI conventions:\n\n**1. OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`)\n- Added `title` as an optional input field on `OwnerFields` (documented values MR/MRS/MS/DR).\n- Added `salutation` as a `readOnly` output field on `Owner`, describing the composition rule.\n- These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n**2. Domain model** (`Owner.java`)\n- Added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter, and included it in `toString()` for parity with the other fields.\n\n**3. Mapping** (`OwnerMapper.java`)\n- Added `formatSalutation(Owner)` \u2014 a small, single-responsibility default method returning `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, or just `lastName` otherwise \u2014 wired via `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", ...)`, matching the existing derived-field pattern (`displayName`, `initials`, etc.).\n- The `title` input maps automatically through MapStruct (name matches on both DTO and entity), so no extra wiring was needed for persistence.\n\n**4. Schema** \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table across all four dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) so it persists between the create and read requests. The test suite uses `hsqldb`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (posts a title of `DR`/lastName `who`, expects `salutation` = `\"DR who\"`) passes, along with the rest of the suite.",
